---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
	LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LICENSE_PATH,
	SITE_BRAND,
	TERMS_PATH,
} from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Refund Policy"
	description="Unused-plan refunds on iStockVisual: refund if you have not downloaded any images. 1-Month Pro includes a 3-day trial."
	heading="Refund Policy"
	lede="You can request a refund only if you have not downloaded any images after purchase. If you have downloaded an image, the plan is used and is not refundable. 1-Month Pro includes a 3-day trial."
>
	<h2>1. Unused plans only</h2>
	<p>
		A refund is available only when the purchase is unused: you have not downloaded any library
		images after paying. If you have downloaded one or more images — at any size, including 500, 1K,
		2K, 4K, or 8K — the plan is used and we do not refund it.
	</p>
	<p>
		This rule applies to Short-Term passes (1-Day, 7-Day, 1-Month) and Long-Term plans (6-Month,
		12-Month, and Lifetime Access). Downloads you made as a free member before that paid purchase do
		not count against the refund.
	</p>
	<p>
		This policy is in addition to any rights you have under consumer law. Those rights are not
		limited by this page.
	</p>

	<h2>2. 1-Day Pass and 7-Day Pass</h2>
	<p>
		These short passes do not include a calendar money-back window. You may request a full refund
		only if you have not downloaded any images after purchase. A single download voids the refund,
		even if the pass has time left.
	</p>

	<h2>3. 1-Month Pro — 3-day trial</h2>
	<p>
		1-Month Pro includes a 3-day trial from the time of purchase. During those 3 days you may
		request a full refund if you have not downloaded any images.
	</p>
	<p>
		After the 3-day trial ends, or after any image download during the trial, the month plan is not
		refundable.
	</p>

	<h2>4. 6-Month, 12-Month, and Lifetime Access</h2>
	<p>
		You may request a refund if you have not downloaded any images after purchase. Once you download
		an image, that plan is not refundable.
	</p>

	<h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
	<p>
		Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address on
		your account. Include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The email on the account</li>
		<li>The plan you bought (for example 1-Day Pass, 1-Month Pro, or Lifetime Access)</li>
		<li>The approximate purchase date</li>
		<li>A short note if something went wrong (optional, but it helps us improve)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We check whether any library downloads occurred after that purchase. Eligible unused refunds are
		returned by the original payment method. We aim to confirm requests promptly.
	</p>

	<h2>6. What happens after a refund</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Pro / pass access on that purchase ends when the refund is issued</li>
		<li>You can still use the site as a free member, including 500 and 1K downloads</li>
		<li>
			Eligible refunds are unused, so there should be no paid downloads on that purchase. Any files
			you already had as a free member remain usable under the
			<a href={LICENSE_PATH}>Content License</a>, including the attribution requirement
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. When we do not refund</h2>
	<p>Except where applicable law requires otherwise, we do not refund:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>A plan after any library image download following that purchase</li>
		<li>1-Month Pro after the 3-day trial, even if you did not download</li>
		<li>Change of mind, unused time, or an expired plan once the purchase is used or the trial has ended</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>8. Chargebacks and abuse</h2>
	<p>
		If you believe a charge is wrong, contact us first so we can help. Filing a chargeback without
		contacting us may delay resolution. We may refuse or claw back a goodwill refund, and may
		suspend accounts, where we see repeated refund abuse, payment fraud, or automated download
		abuse. See also the <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Refund questions for {SITE_BRAND}:
		<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
